 "transcript": [
  "[action] (to the eldest son, the second son) Wang Lung looks at his sons and then at Pear Blossom.",
  "[action] (to the eldest son) The second son returns home.",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"We are setting up a great store and we will make a great deal of money out of it.\"",
  "[silence] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung says nothing.",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"We will sell out the north fields, and there is the pond there and a good well. We can sell that land for a good sum and have enough to start us with.\"",
  "[action] Wang Lung feels the ground",
  "the eldest son (to the eldest son): \"Well, well, and what are you waiting for? What is the good of these lands to you?\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"They are mine!\"",
  "[action] Wang Lung goes to room",
  "the eldest son (to the eldest son, the second son): \"Well, and I will sell them and we will have enough to start us with.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"You cannot sell the land,\"",
  "Wang Lung: \"It is mine, and it shall not be sold without my will.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"My sons, I have lived on this land all my life, and my father and his father before him, and his father's father. I have eaten the rice which this land produced, and I have drunk the water from this land's wells. I have buried my dead in this land, and I have been buried by my sons on this land.\"",
  "Wang Lung: \"Well, and you cannot sell the land when I am dead, for you will have sons of your own and they will sell it, and you will be glad to sell it to eat the rice.\"",
  "[says] The eldest son responds with humility.",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"Well, and it is true, and it is a sad thing that we should not be able to sell it.\"",
  "Wang Lung: \"Now let us walk on the land!\"",
  "[action] The sons walk the land with their father.",
